                    insight_oneoffmiss: 'You designed for the survey week. A one-off push buys a spike in participation and nothing that keeps running after June, so the model cut the return on the whole budget by 38%; here it did not reach 50% even in the window the board reads.',
                    insight_inforeflex: 'You read the gap as an information deficit. The survey had already run that test: the behavior-change rate came in at 21% and 22% in the two preceding cycles, with an information campaign running throughout. A plan built on that reading delivers its frame as facts to people who already agree, so your Round 2 message gains counted for half.',
                    insight_oppositionread: 'You read the workforce as opposed. 71% of them say they care about sustainability; a plan built on requiring change treats supporters as opponents, so your Round 2 message gains counted for half.',
                    insight_factfeeling: 'You answered a feeling with a fact. The worker made a claim about intent, and a roadmap or a dataset answers a question about carbon. The fear left the room and stayed in the workforce, and the works council can slow any change to how a line is run.',
                    insight_multiplier: 'What Rounds 1 to 3 built set the return on every euro in Round 4: your 600.000 € worked at a multiplier of ×{m} (at 1.00 the money returns its face value).',
                    coach_r2_riskmismatch: '<strong>You named a risk that belongs to a frame you did not choose.</strong> Every frame has its own downside. What is the risk of the one you picked, and what would tell you before June that it was going wrong?',
                    coach_r2_misread: '<strong>The frame goes out inside a plan that was not built for it.</strong> In Round 1 the plan did not read the gap as an emotional one, so this frame travels as part of a campaign aimed elsewhere and its gains count for half.',
                    coach_r4_promisedue: '<strong>The guarantee from the town hall has come due.</strong> The board has not made it and the works council is holding you to it: regulation fell 8 points, message effectiveness fell 10 and resistance rose 14 before the budget went to work, so every euro bought less.',
